# Build directories
build/
build-static/
# any local/CI build tree (build-local, build-ci8, build-246gate, ...)
build-*/
dist/

# CMake (generated in build directories)
CMakeCache.txt
CMakeFiles/
cmake_install.cmake
*.cmake
# ...but *.cmake also swallows hand-written CMake scripts that live in the
# SOURCE tree (vms-76e: this one is the body of a ctest, so if it silently
# failed to get committed the test would red in CI with "no such file"
# instead of its real diagnostic).
#
# vms-4847: the per-path allowlist above this comment (one `!` line added by
# hand for each new shim) is exactly the failure mode it was meant to guard
# against -- three of these _no_python3.cmake bodies (and counting) were
# referenced by tests/vmsscs/CMakeLists.txt's else() branch for months and
# never existed in git because nobody remembered to add their line here. One
# of the three failed LOUD (a bare cmake -P "file does not exist" error); the
# rest failed SILENT, indistinguishable from a green run with the gate simply
# absent. Carve out the whole naming convention instead of one path at a
# time, so a new shim needs no .gitignore edit to survive `git add`:
!*_no_python3.cmake
# tests/integration/test_cmake_shims_tracked.sh is the standing gate that
# catches the case this carve-out cannot: a *_no_python3.cmake file that
# exists on disk, is referenced by a CMakeLists.txt else() branch, but was
# never `git add`-ed at all (as opposed to being re-ignored).
!tests/vmsscs/capture_manifest_no_python3.cmake

